# Own-wording items and magic variants of Humblewood Campaign Setting and Humblewood Tales (2014 rules). Row shape as tdcsr_item.py: add(name, type, rarity, attune, text, **opts).
# Mundane gear (rarity none) goes to GEAR rows: name, cost gp, weight lb, type, text. Weapons from baseitem get WDESC only.
# The item groups (Feather Robe, Jerbeen Figurines, Kwark's Wondrous Kernels) are covered by their members.
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

def add(name, typ, rar, att, text, **o):
    ITEMS.append((name, typ, rar, att, text, o))

# ---------------- Campaign Setting
add("Borealus", "Staff", "Artifact", 1,
 "A staff made from the finger of an ancient frost elemental. It is so cold that bare skin goes numb, though an attuned bearer is immune to that. **Gifts of the Rime.** While attuned you have Resistance to fire damage, Immunity to cold damage, and you know the ray of frost cantrip. **Breath of Winter.** As an action while holding it, you breathe a 100 ft cone of hoarfrost. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 18 Constitution save, taking 9d8 cold damage on a fail or half on a success. This works again after the next dawn. **Glacial Prison.** As an action, touch the staff to a surface and raise a barrier of ice from a point you can see on that surface within 200 ft. It acts as a wall of ice cast at 6th level with save DC 18. This works again after 3 days. **Cruel Winds.** A bitter boreal wind follows the staff. It gusts within 30 ft of the attuned bearer and snuffs out nonmagical flames. **Destroying the Staff.** Flames from a fire elemental of equal power to its source can destroy it, melting it away over centuries.",
 fx={"res": ["Fire"], "imm": ["Cold"]}, base=["Quarterstaff"], ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Borealus"] = {"sp": [["Ray of Frost", 0], ["Wall of Ice", 6]], "dc": 18}

add("Feathered Helm", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1,
 "A simple helm of leather, hide, scale, or plate, powered by a gifted feather. Birdfolk treat giving a feather as one of the highest honors, a sign of lasting bond or deep thanks. The helm has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. Its powers depend on the birdfolk who gave the feather, and any save from its spells is DC 16. **Corvum.** 1 charge casts tasha's hideous laughter, 2 charges cast detect thoughts. **Gallus.** 1 charge casts bless, 2 charges cast aid. **Luma.** 1 charge casts a random 1st level sorcerer spell, then roll a d20. On a 20 you can use this again without spending a charge. On a 1 the spell also targets you, unless you are its only target, in which case it fizzles. **Raptor.** 1 charge casts hunter's mark, 2 charges cast magic weapon. **Strig.** 1 charge casts divine favor, 2 charges cast pass without trace. **A True Gift.** The GM should pick the feather type from the character's ties to the birdfolk peoples. A birdfolk player may want to offer the gift themselves, with a real story bond behind it.",
 ch=[3, "1d3", "dawn"])
SP["Feathered Helm"] = {"sp": [["Tasha's Hideous Laughter", 1], ["Detect Thoughts", 2], ["Bless", 1], ["Aid", 2], ["Hunter's Mark", 1], ["Magic Weapon", 2], ["Divine Favor", 1], ["Pass without Trace", 2]], "dc": 16}

add("Necronomicon Ex Corvis", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 1,
 "A one of a kind tome of dark necromancy, written by the mad corvum necromancer Lathrus of the Night's Call. It works as a spellbook, so only wizards truly benefit. **Abyssal Secrets.** After a full week of study your Intelligence rises by 2 and your Wisdom drops by 1. **Grasp of Shadows.** By reciting a ritual from the book for at least a minute, you summon 1d4 + 2 shadows that obey you and follow your orders as best they can. Usable once per week. **Knowledge Beyond Reason.** You can add the spells below to your spellbook even if you cannot yet prepare or cast them, and they become preparable once you reach the right level. Instead of paying gold to copy a spell, you can take 1 damage and gain one level of exhaustion to scribe it in your own blood. 3rd level: animate dead, bestow curse, vampiric touch. 4th level: blight. 6th level: circle of death, magic jar. 7th level: finger of death. **The Corvum's Curse.** After copying at least one spell from the tome, make a DC 16 Wisdom save or be cursed as by bestow curse, with the effect chosen by the GM. It lasts 2d4 days and the timer resets each time you copy another spell from it. Only remove curse cast with a slot of 5th level or higher ends it early. **Destroying the Book.** Unlike other artifacts it can be damaged. Pages torn out lose their magic within a day, and 8 hours of direct sunlight drains all the dark magic from the whole book.",
 by="Wizard", fx={"abil": ["INT", 2, 22]})

add("Nest Charm", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A sphere of interwoven metal branches shaped like a nest. Set it on the ground and speak its command word and it unfolds into a 30 ft wide platform of branches. A magical tree then grows beneath the platform and lifts it 50 ft into the air, carrying everyone and everything on it. The perch lasts up to 8 hours, then the tree sinks back into the ground and the platform curls up into the charm again. Speaking the command word at any time ends it early the same way. After use it works again at the next dawn.",
 ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])

add("Wing Crest Shield", "Armor", "Uncommon", 1,
 "While you wield this shield you gain a +1 bonus to AC on top of the shield's normal bonus. As an action, speak the command word to cast gust of wind (save DC 15). After that it works again at the next dawn.",
 fx={"ac": 1}, base=["Shield"], ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Wing Crest Shield"] = {"sp": [["Gust of Wind", 0]], "dc": 15}

# ---- magic variants
add("Blade of the Wood", "Weapon", "Rare", 1,
 "Any sword. A finely crafted blade with delicate etchings that hums faintly with life. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. It has 2 charges. Spend a charge and speak the command word to cast spike growth (save DC 16) centered on yourself, and you pass through that terrain unharmed. It regains 1 charge each dawn.",
 fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, ch=[2, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Blade of the Wood"] = {"sp": [["Spike Growth", 1]], "dc": 16}

add("Red-Feather Bow", "Weapon", "Uncommon", 1,
 "Any bow. A hunting weapon prized by the mistral raptors, enchanted to help its user watch distant prey. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. It has 3 charges. When you fire an arrow from it, you can speak the command word and spend a charge as a bonus action to see through the arrow. You see from the spot where it lands as if you stood there for 1 minute. If the arrow hits a creature, you instead see what that creature sees for the same time. It regains 1d3 charges each dawn.",
 fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, ch=[3, "1d3", "dawn"])

# ---------------- Tales: wondrous items, rings, rods, staffs
add("Alluring Dye", "Potion", "Common", 0,
 "A thick paste in many colors, from the brightest shades seen on gallus to quieter browns, blacks, and greens. Rubbed into feathers, fur, or hair, it permanently dyes them. For 24 hours after the first use you have +2 to Charisma saves, and you cannot gain this again unless you use a dye of a different color. If you re-dye yourself more than once in ten days, roll a d4. On a 1 the dyes clash, your coloring turns a shocking yellow, and you have Disadvantage on Charisma checks for 1d6 days until it fades.")
add("Antlers of the True Path", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0,
 "A polished wooden divining rod carved as antlers with fine filigree, valued by the seers of Cairith. Hold it by the antlers and spend 10 minutes picturing a person, place, or object you know. The rod then pulls you toward the target for as long as you concentrate on it, as with a spell. It only works if the target is within 1,000 ft and on your plane. After use it works again at the next dawn.",
 ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Band of Fruitfulness", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1,
 "A gold bangle etched with fruits, vegetables, and cooked dishes. It has 6 charges. Speak the command word and spend up to 6 charges and the bangle leaves your wrist and becomes a gold table loaded with fresh, homely food that never spoils and stays full until the effect ends. Up to 5 creatures can sit at it. Each charge spent means 10 minutes of feasting, and everyone who feasts the whole time gains the benefits by charge count. **1:** each heals 5d8 hit points. **2:** also Advantage on saves against Poisoned and Frightened for 1 hour. **3:** also cured of all diseases and poisons affecting them. **4:** also exhaustion reduced by one level. **5:** also hit point maximum up by 2d10 for 1 hour with the same number of hit points gained. **6:** all of the above, exhaustion reduced by one extra level, and the 1 hour benefits last 24 hours. Each charge spent fades some of the etchings, and with no charges left it looks like a plain gold bangle. It regains 2 charges at dawn up to 6. Followers of Hanera value it.",
 by="Bard, cleric or druid", ch=[6, "2", "dawn"])
add("Basilisk Crystal", "Wondrous Item", "Common", 0,
 "Basilisks grow these crystals on their backs and shed them. They are extremely hard and only adamantine tools or weapons can cut or damage them. A basilisk crystal makes an excellent arcane spell focus.")
add("Belt of the Weald", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A thin chain belt that looks metal but is made of tiny links of polished wood. While you wear it, you have Advantage on Survival checks in forests and ignore difficult terrain while moving through forests. You can also cast longstrider on yourself once, and it works again at the next dawn.",
 ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Belt of the Weald"] = {"sp": [["Longstrider", 0]]}
add("Chronicle of Fools", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1,
 "A poorly bound leather journal full of tales from adventurers and chroniclers across centuries. The back pages are always blank and hunger for more stories. The cover cannot be destroyed, and torn or damaged pages regrow within minutes. Nothing written in it can be smudged, hidden, or changed, and only an attuned owner can write in it. As an action, consult its stories to give yourself, or a creature that can hear you, Advantage on one ability check. The target also adds double its Proficiency Bonus to that check unless it already has Expertise in the skill. **Curse.** Attuning curses you. You do not want to part with the book, you feel pushed to keep it on you at all times, and an urge drives you to write detailed, completely honest entries about your life, including private details, weaknesses, flaws, and damaging secrets.")
add("Cloak of Spines", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A cloak of large soft quills that harden when worn. While you wear it and no armor, your AC is 14 plus your Dexterity modifier. When a melee attack hits you, you can use your Reaction to have the cloak block it and strike back. The attack's damage is reduced by 2d4 and the attacker takes 2d4 magical Piercing damage. A hedge doing this reduces the damage by 4d4 and deals 4d4 instead. After use it works again at the next dawn.",
 fx={"acBase": 14}, ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Cogwork Wings", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0,
 "A brass and cloth pair of wings on a box of gears, made by a mapach tinkerer and worn on the back with leather straps. Two levers sit on either side of the mechanism. Before putting it on, pull the left lever to extend the wings and the right to set them flapping. Pushing the right stops the flapping and pushing the left retracts them, but you cannot reach the levers while wearing it. While you wear the wings in motion you have a Fly Speed set by your weight, using total weight with gear worn and carried (the 20 lb wings are included). Under 150 lb: fly 60 ft, glide descent 30 ft. 150 to 250 lb: fly 30 ft, glide descent 60 ft. Over 250 lb: no flight and no glide. You can fly up to 1 hour in total, in one trip or several, and each flight counts rounded up to the next minute. If you are flying when the hour ends, the wings stop and you fall. As a Reaction while falling, press the button on the front of the strap buckle to lock the wings and glide, descending the listed number of feet per round while moving forward at the same pace. Pressing it has a 50 percent chance of jamming the wings in the glide position. If that happens the device is useless after you land until it frees itself after 2d12 hours. The wings regain 10 minutes of flight for every 4 hours not in use.",
 fx={"fly": 60})

_ROBE = "A luxuriant robe made from the feather of a birdfolk spellcaster. It looks like many plumes but is really one feather copied again and again by its magic. While you wear it, your Intelligence or Charisma becomes 22 (choose when you first attune) and you gain a +1 bonus to saving throws. "
for _n, _t in (("Corvum", "Your spell attacks have Advantage against foes that have not yet acted in this combat. A successful spell attack against a surprised creature counts as a Critical Hit."),
               ("Gallus", "When you cast a spell that targets only one ally and does not have a range of self, you can target a second ally in range with the same spell. You can do this up to three times a day."),
               ("Luma", "When a target succeeds on a saving throw against one of your spells, you can use your Reaction to make it roll the save again, and it must keep the new result. You can do this up to three times a day."),
               ("Raptor", "When you cast a spell that damages a single target and you have already spent some of your movement this turn, the spell deals extra damage equal to your character level."),
               ("Strig", "Your spell attacks have Advantage against foes that have not yet acted in this combat. A successful spell attack against a surprised creature counts as a Critical Hit.")):
    add(_n + " Feather Robe", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1, _ROBE + _t, by="Sorcerer, warlock or wizard", fx={"save": 1})

add("Cream of Ooze Moisturizing Face Serum", "Potion", "Common", 0,
 "A light pink cream. Rubbed on your face or a similar sized patch of skin, it works like prestidigitation and cleans away grime and dirt.")
add("Crown of Daffodils", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A woven crown of leafy flowering vines that sprouts 1d4 blooming daffodils. While at least one daffodil is in bloom on it and you wear it, you gain a +1 bonus to ability checks and saving throws. As an action you can pluck a daffodil and give it to another creature, who can magically fix it on themselves as a boutonniere, hair ornament, or corsage. While holding a fresh daffodil, that creature also gets +1 to ability checks and saving throws. A plucked flower withers after 1 hour and stops working. Each dawn 1d4 daffodils bloom on the crown, up to 4. When the last daffodil is removed, roll a d20. On a 1 the crown withers away and is destroyed.",
 fx={"save": 1}, ch=[4, "1d4", "dawn"])
add("Draught of Feather Shine", "Potion", "Very Rare", 0,
 "An oily draught. When you drink it, you have Advantage on Charisma ability checks and saving throws for 24 hours. If you have feathers, they gleam more than usual.")
add("Draught of Slime Curse Cure", "Potion", "Rare", 0,
 "A thick, bubbly, slightly sour green liquid. Drinking it gives you the benefit of remove curse as if cast on you, and Advantage on saves against being cursed for 1 hour afterward.")
add("Egg of Rebirth", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", 1,
 "A smooth golden egg that fits in one hand, warm and surprisingly sturdy, blessed with the life giving power of Ardea. Attuning to it places a portion of your life energy inside. You then always know its direction and distance while you share a plane with it. It cannot be broken or destroyed. Only power word kill cast on it destroys it, and then it turns black and crumbles to dust and kills any attuned character no matter their hit points. While you carry it, you can use your Reaction to give yourself Advantage on a saving throw against one effect or condition currently affecting you. After use it works again at the next dawn. If you die while the egg is within 20 ft, it shatters and you return to life in a burst of bright light, restored to full hit points with your hit point maximum restored if it had been reduced. All hostile creatures within 60 ft must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution save or take 12d6 radiant damage, half as much on a success. Any creature that fails is Blinded for 1 minute.",
 ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Eye of Starsight", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1,
 "A black bronze amulet of fine cogwork with a polished glass orb the size of an eye in its center. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 each night at dusk. **Cosmic Insight.** While you wear it, when you make a skill check, attack roll, or saving throw, you can use your Reaction and spend a charge to roll again. Do it after the first die is rolled but before the result is known, and you must take the new roll. **Stellar Eye.** Speaking a command word opens the cogwork slightly so the orb can be taken out, and speaking it again closes it. While open, you can use a bonus action to make the orb float out of its setting or go back to rest. While it floats, you can use an action to move it up to 30 ft in any direction, and you can spend 1 charge to receive its sight in your mind for 10 minutes. The orb has truesight to 30 ft, is blind beyond that, and sees in all directions at once. It can travel any distance from you but not onto another plane. Solid barriers block it, but it can pass through an opening as narrow as 1 inch. While the orb is out of the amulet, you cannot use the other property.",
 ch=[3, "1d3", "dusk"])
add("Fangs of Guile", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1,
 "A rare necklace made by supplicants of Kren, who learned the craft in a ritual exchange. It gives its wearer equal parts guile and ferocity. While you wear it, you have Advantage on Deception, Insight, and Persuasion checks. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 each night at dusk. As an action you can spend 1 to 3 charges and a large red spectral maw bites a creature you can see within 5 ft. It makes an attack roll with a +7 bonus. On a hit the target takes 3d6 magical Piercing damage for each charge spent, and you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. If the necklace has no charges at dusk, roll 1d6. On a 1 the fangs yellow and dull, and the necklace loses its magic forever.",
 ch=[3, "1d3", "dusk"])
add("Flame of Ingenuity", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1,
 "A wooden lantern holding a small flame that shows the true power of fire when properly harnessed. The first one is said to have been inspired by Gesme herself. **Light of Revelation.** The flame never goes out and can only be quenched inside an antimagic field. It gives bright light in a 30 ft radius and dim light for another 30 ft. Invisible creatures and objects become visible in its light, and illusions in the light are revealed as spectral forms rather than solid things. As a bonus action, speak a command word to shrink the flame to dim light in a 5 ft radius. **Stroke of Ingenuity.** While attuned, when you roll a 1 or 2 on an Intelligence check, you can roll again and must use the new result. **Arcane Rekindling.** By meditating on the flame for 1 minute, you regain spell slots totaling up to 5 levels, divided as you like. For example, one 5th level slot, or one 3rd and one 2nd. This works again after the next dawn.",
 by="Bard, sorcerer or wizard", ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Glowing Ember", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0,
 "A clear 1 lb crystal with an ember hanging in its center, always warm to the touch. Speak its command word within 60 ft and the ember glows, shedding bright light and heat in a 20 ft radius and dim light for another 20 ft. Creatures within 20 ft feel the heat and have Resistance to cold damage while it glows. Speaking the word again puts it out. A solid object such as a bucket or barrel placed over it blocks the light but not the heat. A second command word makes the crystal float up to 5 ft off the ground, and speaking it again stops the floating. If you move more than 20 ft from the hovering crystal, it follows you by the shortest path, avoiding obstacles if it can, until it is within 20 ft. If it is lit and cannot reach the creature it follows within 3 rounds, it grows hotter and then explodes, dealing 8d6 fire damage to each creature within 20 ft and destroying itself. A creature caught in the blast makes a DC 13 Dexterity save for half damage. While lit, the crystal can be attacked. It is a Tiny object with 30 hit points, AC 16, Resistance to nonmagical slashing and piercing damage, and Immunity to fire damage. At 0 hit points it explodes as described.")
add("Kwark's Wondrous Kernels, Planter", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0,
 "Kernels about an inch across in many shapes and colors, found in plain velvet pouches holding 2d4 seeds. Each bag is all planters or all tossables, never both. The GM rolls a d8 to find what the bag holds or picks from the list. A planter kernel must be planted. As an action, plant a seed in nearby soil and 1 minute later its effect appears. Everything it creates rots into organic mush 1 hour after sprouting, including any removable parts. **1, Round Black:** A Large red flower grows. It swallows the first Large or smaller creature that comes within 5 ft of it on a turn for the first time. The swallowed creature is Restrained and Blinded and has cover from outside effects. It holds one creature at a time. A swallowed creature can cut free with a slashing weapon from the inside. The flower has AC 14 and 30 hit points and withers at 0, freeing its prisoner. **2, Oval Yellow:** A strong root rises with a removable wooden knob like a bottle stopper. It works as an eversmoking bottle once an action removes the knob, but the smoke is yellow and smells of mustard. **3, Teardrop Brown:** A small tree grows with 1d4 + 1 red fruits. Eating one as an action gives the benefit of a potion of healing. **4, Teardrop Orange:** A sturdy sapling grows with one long, easily removed branch. Anyone holding it can make it glow or stop. It sheds bright orange light in a 60 ft radius and dim light for another 60 ft. **5, Round Red:** A wooden shaft shoots up and ignites. This magical torch can be pulled up and wielded, shedding bright red light in a 30 ft radius and dim light for another 30 ft. Attack with it as a club. A creature hit takes extra 2d6 fire damage and must make a DC 13 Dexterity save or catch fire, taking 1d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. It can repeat the save using an action to end it. Only magic can put out the torch. **6, Oval Russet:** A hollow seed shell grows and splits in two halves, each usable as a standard shield. Anyone wielding one has Resistance to fire damage. **7, Heart Green:** A gnarled staff wrapped in ivy and fruiting grapevines grows. It can be taken and used as a quarterstaff, and it counts as under a shillelagh spell as long as it exists. **8, Teardrop Purple:** A Huge mushroom grows with a wooden door in its stalk and a small stone chimney on top. Inside are a stone hearth and five soft cushions. Whoever planted the seed can mentally lock or unlock the door at any time.")
add("Kwark's Wondrous Kernels, Tossable", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0,
 "Kernels about an inch across in many shapes and colors, found in plain velvet pouches holding 2d4 seeds. Each bag is all tossables or all planters, never both. The GM rolls a d8 to find what the bag holds or picks from the list. A tossable kernel is triggered by throwing it. As an action, throw a kernel up to 20 ft. Its effect is instant and uses up the seed. **1, Round Black:** A haze of blue pollen bursts. Each creature within 10 ft must make a DC 13 Constitution save or fall unconscious. A sleeper can be woken by an action and wakes if it takes damage. Otherwise it wakes in 1 minute. **2, Oval Yellow:** A 10 ft radius cloud of stinking yellow gas lasts 1 minute and otherwise matches stinking cloud (save DC 14). **3, Teardrop Brown:** A gentle green glow. Each creature within 10 ft gains 2d4 + 2 Temporary Hit Points. **4, Teardrop Orange:** A burst of orange acid. Each creature within 10 ft must succeed on a DC 14 Dexterity save or take 2d8 acid damage. **5, Round Red:** The seed explodes in flame. Each creature within 10 ft makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 5d6 fire damage on a fail or half on a success. **6, Oval Russet:** A cloud of small brown burrs. Each creature within 10 ft is coated and has Vulnerability to fire damage for 1 minute. **7, Heart Green:** A cloud of pink floral mist. Each creature within 10 ft must make a DC 14 Wisdom save or be unable to attack or take hostile actions for 1 minute. It can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, and the effect ends at once if it is attacked. **8, Teardrop Purple:** A haze of befuddling spores. Each creature within 5 ft must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save or act as if under confusion. At the end of each of its turns it can repeat the save to end the effect.")
add("Marotte of Chance", "Rod", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A flashy bird shaped jester's baton filled with the magic of the Amaranthine Clhuran, the magic of fate. Lumas can draw on it for many effects. It serves as an arcane spell focus and has an odd heft. It works as a magical club for which you use your Charisma modifier for attack and damage rolls. Each time you hit with it, roll a d100. On a 10 or less something odd happens, so roll a d10 on the Chance Table for an extra effect. The attack deals normal damage unless the result says otherwise. **1:** No damage and a loud squeak heard to 100 ft. **2:** A bouquet of sweet flowers sprouts from the head. No damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Charmed by you for 1 minute. The charm ends when you or an ally takes a hostile action against it. **3:** You and the target swap places by teleport with an audible pop. **4:** Lightning arcs at the target for 2d6 lightning damage. Each creature within 10 ft of the target, including you, makes a DC 13 Dexterity save or takes 1d6 lightning damage. **5:** The target is affected by enlarge/reduce. On an even d10 it is enlarged and on an odd roll it is reduced. An unwilling target can avoid it with a DC 13 Constitution save. **6:** The marotte becomes a greataxe. The attack deals 1d12 + your Charisma modifier slashing damage instead of its usual damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or be Frightened of you for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. It returns to normal at the start of your next turn. **7:** The target glows a color you choose until the start of your next turn, sheds bright light in a 15 ft radius and dim light for another 15 ft, and cannot be invisible. **8:** You turn invisible for 1 minute. Roll a d10 and on an odd result the target is invisible for 1 minute too. **9:** No damage. The target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or turn into a frog for 1 minute as under polymorph. Roll another d10 and on a 1 the effect happens again and targets you. **10:** Roll twice more, ignoring 10s, and apply both results. A no damage result removes only the attack's original damage, not damage from other effects.",
 by="Luma", fx={"atk": 0})
add("Pathfinder's Pebble", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1,
 "A polished pebble marked with the holy symbol of Reya and blessed by the Amaranthine. While you carry it outdoors, you always know which way is north. Holding it, you can spend an action to focus on your surroundings and cast commune with nature once. It works again each dawn. You can also grip it and say aloud the name of a fixed location you know on your plane. You learn the shortest, most direct physical route there (not necessarily the safest), how far it is, and which way it lies, for as long as you hold the pebble. This lasts until you arrive, choose a new destination the same way, or dismiss it at no action cost.",
 by="Cleric of the nature domain, druid or ranger", ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Pathfinder's Pebble"] = {"sp": [["Commune with Nature", 0]]}
add("Potion of Rest", "Potion", "Rare", 0,
 "A pale blue elixir with a jasmine flower floating in it, brewed with Swarm of Bluebees venom that helps the drinker sleep calmly and deeply. Drink it before a short or long rest and you wake with 1d10 + 5 Temporary Hit Points and with one level of exhaustion removed. This is in addition to what the rest gives you.")
add("Recall Crystal", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0,
 "A small clear crystal. As an action, smash it to teleport yourself and all equipment you wear or hold to the Alderheart council chambers. It is destroyed when used.")
add("Ring of Plant Speech", "Ring", "Uncommon", 0,
 "While you wear this ring, you can speak with plants and plant creatures within 30 ft as if you shared a language. Nonsentient plants within 30 ft gain awareness and speak to you telepathically. You can ask them about events from the last day and learn about passing creatures, weather, and other happenings nearby, from the plant's narrow viewpoint. Followers of Henwin prize this ring.")
add("Ring of the Sky Hunter", "Ring", "Rare", 1,
 "A ring whose dark metal talons grasp a blue gem that swirls with windblown clouds. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 spent charges each dawn. **Stooping Talons.** While you wear it, you can use an action and spend any number of charges to attack one creature you can see within 60 ft. A pair of spectral talons dives from the sky and makes an attack roll with a +7 bonus. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 magical Piercing damage for each charge spent. **Raising Talons.** Instead, you can spend 1 to 3 charges as an action to have the talons lift a Large or smaller creature you can see within 60 ft. The target is Grappled and lifted 20 ft into the air per charge spent. An unwilling target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save to avoid it. The grapple lasts a number of rounds equal to the charges spent. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns to break free, and takes falling damage as normal if it does.",
 ch=[3, "1d3", "dawn"])
add("Shroud of Ending", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 1,
 "**Attunement.** When you attune, make a DC 12 Constitution save. On a fail the shroud ages you 5d10 years. For the next hour you have Disadvantage on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws. If this ages you past your race's average natural lifespan, you die at once and your soul rises as a ghost sworn to guard the artifact. While attuned, you deal 1d6 necrotic damage to any plant you touch that is not a creature, plant and beast creatures within 30 ft become hostile to you, and you stop aging and need no food or sleep. When you stop being attuned, you immediately age by the time you would have aged while attuned, and you die if that exceeds your race's average natural lifespan. **Blessings of Tyton.** While you wear the cloak you gain a +2 bonus to AC and saving throws, see in darkness as if it were bright light, are immune to poison damage, the Poisoned condition, and all diseases, and have Advantage on death saves and on saves against effects that would kill you outright. **Hasten the Sunset.** As an action, force a living creature you can see within 120 ft to age rapidly. It makes a DC 17 Constitution save, aging 6d10 years on a fail and 1 year on a success. On a fail it is also cursed. It automatically fails Strength and Dexterity checks and has Disadvantage on all other attack rolls, ability checks, and saves, until remove curse is cast on it. A target aged past its race's average lifespan dies. This works again after a week. **Shade's Form.** You can cast etherealness. This works again after the next dusk. **Step of the Night's Shadow.** As an action, teleport to a spot you choose within 500 ft that is in bright or dim light. It can be a place you see, one you picture, or one you describe by distance and direction, such as 200 ft straight down or 300 ft up to the northwest at 45 degrees. If the spot is not lit, you arrive at the nearest lit spot in range, and the teleport fails if there is none. You can bring objects up to what you can carry and one willing creature of your size or smaller within 5 ft that carries gear up to its capacity. If the spot is occupied by an object or creature, the teleport fails. After you use it, roll 1d6, and on a 1 you cannot use it again until the next dusk. **Destroying the Cloak.** Only a cleric of Ardea of at least 17th level can destroy it, by presenting it to the rising sun, praying to return the power of night and death to Tyton, and casting daylight on the cloak. When Ardea's dawn comes, the shroud's power returns to Tyton's realm and leaves behind a faintly magical but powerless cloak that looks like the dusk sky.",
 fx={"ac": 2, "save": 2, "imm": ["Poison"], "condImm": ["Poisoned"]}, ch=[1, "1", "dusk"])
SP["Shroud of Ending"] = {"sp": [["Etherealness", 0]]}
add("Slimeforged Blade", "Weapon", "Very Rare", 0,
 "A greatsword with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. When you attack a creature with it and roll a natural 20, the target is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn.",
 fx={"atk": 2, "dmg": 2}, base=["Greatsword"])
add("Staff of Climbing Ivy", "Staff", "Uncommon", 1,
 "A staff of several leafy vines grown together into a twisted walking stick, rigid and sturdy. It has three command words and you must hold it to use them. **Growth.** As a bonus action, up to 120 ft of creeping vines grow from the staff toward a solid surface or unattended object you can see, at 30 ft per round. **Grasp.** Speaking the second word, which takes no action, makes the vines fix firmly to a surface or unattended object in reach. They anchor to only one at a time. **Grapple.** As an action, speak the third word and the vines retract at 30 ft per round. If anchored to a solid surface, they pull the wielder toward it at the same speed. If anchored to an object, they pull the object to the wielder. Extended vines can be attacked. They have AC 14, 45 hit points, Vulnerability to fire and slashing damage, Strength 16, and can bear 240 lb. More weight starts to tear them, dealing 10 damage to them each round. If the vines reach 0 hit points, the staff is destroyed. They regain all hit points when they retract.",
 by="Bard, druid, sorcerer or warlock", base=["Quarterstaff"])
add("Talon Tincture", "Potion", "Very Rare", 0,
 "A light tincture. Apply it to your talons, claws, or other limbs and you have Advantage on Dexterity ability checks and saving throws for 24 hours.")
add("Talons of the Squall", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1,
 "Leg bracers given to those who pass the test of endurance run by the priests of Altus. They crackle with faint energy. While you wear them, you have Resistance to lightning damage and Advantage on saves and ability checks to resist being moved by strong winds. Strong winds, heavy rain, and heavy snow do not impose Disadvantage on your ranged attack rolls or Perception checks, and if you can fly you fly at normal speed in such conditions.",
 fx={"res": ["Lightning"]})
add("The Thorn of Kren", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 1,
 "A pitch black thorn that thrums with eldritch power. When you touch it, you must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom save or become attuned to it automatically. If that would exceed your attunement limit, the GM chooses one of your attuned items to end at once. Handling it with gloves or wrapped in cloth avoids this. **Hunter Senses.** While attuned you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks. **Bite.** Your teeth sharpen into a natural weapon. Make unarmed strikes with it against creatures within 5 ft, using your Strength or Dexterity modifier. It deals 1d8 piercing damage, and you can attack with it as a bonus action on each of your turns. **Vicious Nature.** You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls with unarmed strikes and natural melee weapons. This does not stack with bonuses from other magic items. **Curse.** The Amaranthine Kren cursed this item, and attuning spreads the curse to you. You are driven by endless hunger and gain this flaw: my hunger is never satisfied, and I must feast on the flesh of beasts at every chance. For every hour you go without fresh beast meat, you must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or fall into bloodlust. In that frenzy you have Disadvantage on all ability checks unrelated to hunting fresh meat. In combat with a beast you have Advantage on attacks, but all attacks against you also have Advantage. Each hour you hold off the frenzy adds 1 to the save DC. After you give in and feed, the DC drops back to 13. **Destroying the Thorn.** It takes a complex ritual known only to ancient orders such as the Tenders. The thorn is placed at the heart of an Evertree and the tree's natural magic purifies it. Otherwise only a wish spell can destroy it.",
 fx={"atk": 2, "dmg": 2})
add("Whistle of Freedom", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0,
 "A captain's whistle. When blown, every creature within 100 ft that can hear it has Advantage on its next saving throw against a spell or effect currently affecting it. Any creature that hears it while under a mind controlling effect, such as dominate person, is freed at once. A creature that benefits from the whistle cannot benefit from it again for 24 hours.")

# ---- Tales magic variant
add("Saber of Unity", "Weapon", "Very Rare", 1,
 "A rapier or scimitar infused with the spirit of Gaspard's leadership, giving its wielder a share of his courage. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. You and any allies within 10 ft of you are immune to the Frightened condition while you wield it. When you score a Critical Hit with it against a foe one size larger than you, you and all allies within 10 ft gain 2d10 Temporary Hit Points.",
 fx={"atk": 2, "dmg": 2, "condImm": ["Frightened"]})

